* SET - CP/M FILE AND DISK ATTRIBUTES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* SET - CP/M FILE AND DISK ATTRIBUTES

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:SET filespec [attributes]
    SYSUTLS:SET drive: [options]

Displays or changes CP/M attributes, disk labels, modes, timestamps and
password-related settings. Example inspection: SYSUTLS:SET I0:TEST.TXT

[RO] and [RW] change file write protection; [SYS] and [DIR] change
directory visibility. CP/M file attributes are distinct from the BYE DU
permission map. Use AUTH to review caller authorization; do not make a
private utility public merely by changing visibility.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
